From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: p9320: no thermal zone on the die temperature

The P9320 reports its die temperature only while a pad powers it; off a
pad the property returns -ENODATA. The power supply core still
registered a thermal zone on it, which failed its first read at boot,
was rechecked with growing delays and disabled after about four
minutes. Nothing uses the zone. Do not register it.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/p9320_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/p9320_charger.c
index dc258c2..69a6714 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/p9320_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/p9320_charger.c
@@ -886,6 +886,12 @@ static const struct power_supply_desc p9320_psy_desc = {
 	.properties = p9320_props,
 	.num_properties = ARRAY_SIZE(p9320_props),
 	.get_property = p9320_get_property,
+	/*
+	 * The die temperature exists only while a pad powers the receiver:
+	 * a thermal zone on it would be polled for data until the core gives
+	 * up and disables it.
+	 */
+	.no_thermal = true,
 };
 
 static int p9320_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
